                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Does \"CXL\" count as a protocol?  How do you differentiate between PCIe and CXL when they use the same PHY?  Fundamentally, I'm asking, \"what is a protocol?\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Connector/Port.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "CXL will count as a protocol - the interconnect protocol that's being transferred on this port (also how this is defined in the Redfish Port schema).\n\nIn case of CXL/PCIe, application layers would be able to determine if CXL was the negotiated protocol?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Connector/Port.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 18,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "I believe my reponse above answers the question, so resolving this. Please repoen if you're expecting further updates to the response/PDI."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Inventory/Connector/Port.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "nit: PCIe"
